# What must NOT be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# THE ONE THAT MATTERS IS `workers/`. The serverless bundle is already about
# 97 MB and is implicated in the cold-start 502s; the Studio workers exist to
# drive ffmpeg over multi-gigabyte video on a Mac Mini, and nothing in that
# tree can run on a read-only serverless filesystem or finish inside a function
# timeout. Media tooling and model weights must never enter this bundle.
#
# AN IGNORE FILE NOBODY VERIFIES IS AN IGNORE FILE THAT STOPS WORKING SILENTLY,
# so this file is not the guard on its own — `npm run check:vercel-bundle`
# (scripts/check_vercel_bundle.cjs, a CI gate) fails the build if these rules
# stop excluding `workers/`, or if anything Vercel actually serves starts
# requiring a file in there. Exclusion and unreachability are two different
# claims and both are checked.
workers/

# Agent worktrees and CI definitions. Neither is reachable from a served route
# and neither has any business in a function bundle. Kept to these two on
# purpose: this file is a SAFETY guard, and a speculative exclusion that turns
# out to be wrong fails in production rather than in CI.
.claude/
.github/
